      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add Kimi K2 usage dashboard shortcut",
        "body": "## Summary\n- expose Kimi K2 in the Usage Dashboard submenu\n- link the dashboard action to `https://kimi-k2.ai/api/user/credits`, the same host/path the credits fetcher polls\n\n## Proof\n\nDeterministic test run on this branch (no network, no credentials):\n\n```text\n$ swift test --disable-sandbox --filter 'MenuDescriptorKimiK2Tests|ProviderMetadataStatusLinkTests'\n✔ Test \"kimi K2 metadata identifies the unofficial provider and its dashboard\" passed\n✔ Test \"kimi K2 menu exposes the usage dashboard action\" passed\n✔ Test run with 3 tests in 2 suites passed.\n```\n\n## Open question for the maintainer — please advise\n\nThe linked URL is the **authenticated API endpoint** that `KimiK2UsageFetcher` polls with `Authorization: Bearer <apiKey>`. The menu's `openDashboard` action opens it in a browser via `NSWorkspace` with **no auth headers**, so a no-auth request returns HTTP 401 (confirmed by curl). The shortcut may still work for a user logged into kimi-k2.ai in their browser (cookie auth), but it is not a confirmed human-readable credits page.\n\nThis also reverts the deliberate decision in #967 to keep `KimiK2` `dashboardURL` nil, to avoid presenting the unofficial `kimi-k2.ai` endpoint as an official surface. `docs/kimi-k2.md` recommends the Moonshot/Kimi provider for the official billing surface, and an earlier Codex review suggested `https://kimrel.com/my-credits` as the human usage page. I could not verify the correct browser URL without a live account, so I'm flagging rather than guessing. Options:\n\n1. Keep `https://kimi-k2.ai/api/user/credits` (works only for cookie-authenticated browser sessions).\n2. Switch to `https://kimrel.com/my-credits` (the human page suggested by the Codex review).\n3. Revert `dashboardURL` to nil (preserves the #967 decision — no shortcut).\n\n## Codex review follow-up\n\nThe earlier review flagged a host mismatch (dashboard vs. fetcher host). The descriptor and metadata both point at `https://kimi-k2.ai/api/user/credits`, matching `KimiK2UsageFetcher.creditsURL`, and the metadata test was aligned to that value (it was stale at `https://kimi-k2.ai/` and failing).\n\n## Testing\n- `swift test --disable-sandbox --filter 'MenuDescriptorKimiK2Tests|ProviderMetadataStatusLinkTests'` (3 passed)\n- `swift build` clean\n",
